		For element: Header cell
			Vertical: bottom
			Typography:
				Bold: true
	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Vertical alignment in a cell
		Paragraph: A cell is stretched to the height of its row. `Vertical` says where its content goes in that height: `top` (the default), `center` or `bottom`. Here the header cells take `Vertical: bottom` from a rule.
			Style: intro
		Table:
			Column sizes: * 90 90 90
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Cell: The tallest cell of the header sets the height of the row, and the others go down
					Cell: Vertical: top
					Cell: Vertical: center
					Cell: Vertical: bottom
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Cell: This long text, in several lines, makes the row taller than the three short cells beside it, which place their content in the height that is left.
					Cell: top
						Vertical: top
					Cell: center
						Vertical: center
					Cell: bottom
						Vertical: bottom
